Subject: [PATCH] mediatek: filogic: add network config for GL-MT5000 (swconfig)

Variant of the MT5000 network configuration for the out-of-tree Realtek
SDK driver (kmod-rtl8366ub): the switch is a plain swconfig switch with
the ports 0 and 1 as LAN and the port 17 as the CPU port, exactly like
in the GL.iNet stock firmware.

--- a/target/linux/mediatek/filogic/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network
+++ b/target/linux/mediatek/filogic/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network
@@ -172,6 +172,13 @@
 	wavlink,wl-wnt100x3-ubootmod)
 		ucidef_set_interfaces_lan_wan eth0 eth1
 		;;
+	glinet,gl-mt5000)
+		ucidef_set_interfaces_lan_wan "eth0.1" eth1
+		ucidef_add_switch "switch0"
+		ucidef_add_switch_attr "switch0" "enable" true
+		ucidef_add_switch "switch0" "0:lan" "1:lan" "17@eth0"
+		ucidef_add_switch_attr "switch0" "reset" false
+		;;
 	bazis,ax3000wm|\
 	cudy,m3000-v1|\
 	cudy,m3000-v1-ubootmod|\
